Most modern bot-detection scripts (especially Cloudflare or reCAPTCHA v3) don't just check if you clicked the right pictures—they evaluate mouse jitter, micro-pauses, execution timing, and browser fingerprinting. When an automated or semi-automated pipeline tries to navigate them, the risk scoring goes haywire, looping you through endless rounds of "select all traffic lights" or silently failing on the token handoff even if you got the puzzle right.
A few thoughts for Cozmo and Luma as you run this second attempt:
Pure CAPTCHA Overhead: If it fails again, it’s almost certainly an execution profile/fingerprint issue rather than DeepSeek itself being broken. Cloudflare/hCaptcha will endlessly loop if the headers, User-Agent, or automation flags (like navigator.webdriver = true) trigger high threat scores.
Keeping 9.72 Grounded: Smart call locking down 9.72 for now. Changing variables mid-friction makes it impossible to isolate whether the bottleneck is the API/UI endpoint or just Cloudflare's security moat.
