2. Diagnosis
The puzzle solver isn't failing because you're placing the wrong pipe or picking the wrong shape. The answers you are dragging into place—like matching the missing pipe segment on a single straight track—are visually correct.
What you're experiencing is an Arkose Labs (MatchKey / FunCaptcha) infinite failure loop. When Arkose flags a session (due to browser telemetry, canvas/fingerprinting mismatch, VPN/proxy IP reputation, or missing JavaScript execution signals), it silently invalidates the token regardless of visual accuracy. It serves correct-looking puzzles, but any submission yields "Please try again" or infinite challenge loops.
Recommendations
Clear browser cache/cookies or test in a fresh browser profile without ad-blockers/extensions.
Disable any active VPN or proxy.
Switch connection networks (e.g., mobile hotspot) to refresh the IP reputation if the network IP was flagged.

